  "黄石最强招牌、必去；停车场小常要等位，最佳半俯视角度在 Fairy Falls 步道上。": "Yellowstone's headline sight and a must-see. The lot is small and you often wait for a spot. The best elevated view is from the Fairy Falls Trail.",
  "必去，留 2 小时；喷发预测挺准但可能晚几分钟，别先去别处再赶回来。": "A must-see; allow 2 hours. Eruption predictions are fairly accurate but can run a few minutes late, so don't leave for somewhere else and try to rush back.",
  "走到牵牛花池要花不少时间，博主觉得观感一般，赶时间可以不去。": "Walking out to Morning Glory Pool takes a good while, and the writer found it underwhelming. Skip it if you're short on time.",
  "值得一去，半小时；就在大棱镜北边，别把两处搞混。": "Worth a stop; half an hour. It's just north of Grand Prismatic, so don't mix the two up.",
  "值得一去，约 1.5 小时；可以开到上层停车少走路，北边山路偶尔被过路野牛堵住。": "Worth a stop; about 1.5 hours. You can drive to the upper terrace parking to cut down on walking. The mountain road to the north is sometimes blocked by passing bison.",
  "黄石大峡谷南北两岸的观景台都能开车直达，下车就看，不用爬山。": "Overlooks on both the north and south rims of the Grand Canyon of the Yellowstone are right by the road. Step out of the car and look; no climbing needed.",
  "博主心目中最好看的间歇泉盆地：精华 1 小时，全部看完至少 2 小时。": "The writer's favorite geyser basin. The highlights take an hour; seeing all of it takes at least 2 hours.",
  "泉一般，但紧挨黄石湖、风景好，是“值得一去”里最可有可无的。": "The hot springs are ordinary, but it sits right on Yellowstone Lake with lovely views. Of the “worth it” stops, it's the easiest to skip.",
  "开车路过靠边停一下就行，不划船不用久留。": "Pull over briefly as you drive by. Unless you're boating, there's no need to linger.",
  "博主很喜欢：弯弯曲曲的小河、牛轭湖，还能看到野牛。": "A favorite of the writer: a winding stream, oxbow lakes, and bison.",
  "可去可不去，主要是闻一闻硫化氢的臭鸡蛋味，算奇景不算美景。": "Optional. It's mostly a chance to smell the rotten-egg hydrogen sulfide: more of a curiosity than a beauty spot.",
  "勉强好看，走下来约 1 小时，博主觉得没必要专门去。": "Pleasant enough; about an hour to walk. The writer doesn't think it's worth a special trip.",
  "提顿公园路离雪山近、停车点多，有的湖能开到湖边；外侧的 191 号公路更适合开车看风景。": "Teton Park Road runs close to the peaks, has plenty of pullouts, and lets you drive right down to some of the lakes. US 191, farther out, is better for a scenic drive.",
  "博主飞科迪租车：科迪机场的 Budget、Hertz 都不许异地还车，最后要开回原地；一落地就要取车，小镇没有 Uber，也没有公共交通。": "The writer flew into Cody and rented a car. Neither Budget nor Hertz at the Cody airport allows one-way rentals, so you have to drive back at the end. Pick up your car as soon as you land: the town has no Uber and no public transit.",
  "强烈推荐住西黄石镇，离西侧的主要景点近；科迪离东门就要 1 小时，不推荐；杰克逊漂亮但贵，适合配大提顿。": "Staying in West Yellowstone is strongly recommended, since it's close to the main sights on the west side. Cody is an hour from the East Entrance alone, so it isn't recommended. Jackson is lovely but expensive, and works best with Grand Teton.",
  "网上买的门票要提前把邮件附件里的二维码存进手机，公园门口没信号。": "If you buy your entrance pass online, save the QR code from the email attachment to your phone ahead of time. There's no signal at the entrance station.",
  "园内基本没信号，提前在谷歌地图下载离线地图（博主说苹果地图下不了）；每天出发前看官网的道路开放图。": "There's almost no cell signal in the park. Download offline maps in Google Maps before you go (the writer says Apple Maps can't do it), and check the park website's road status map before setting out each day.",
  "园内没看到卖吃的，每天出发前买好午饭和水，车上再备些吃喝以防抛锚。": "The writer didn't find food for sale in the park. Buy lunch and water before heading out each day, and keep extra food and drinks in the car in case of a breakdown.",
  "黄石玩 2–3 天、每天两三个点最舒服，再给大提顿一天；5 月中下旬人少、还能看到雪山，但要带厚外套。": "Two to three days in Yellowstone with two or three stops a day is the most comfortable pace, plus a day for Grand Teton. Mid- to late May is quieter and the peaks still have snow, but bring a warm jacket.",
  "去过 4 次，都在秋冬": "Four visits, all in fall or winter",
  "把优胜美地山谷分成三种玩法：开车沿单行环线停 7 个经典观景点、走 3 条瀑布徒步线、住 3 种住宿。她下次想挑 5 月底来，那时融雪让瀑布水量最大。": "Yosemite Valley in three parts: a drive around the one-way loop with seven classic viewpoints, three waterfall hikes, and three kinds of lodging. Next time she wants to come in late May, when snowmelt puts the falls at their fullest.",
  "山谷单行环线（逆时针）": "Valley one-way loop (counterclockwise)",
