  "Boyden 溶洞": "Boyden Cavern",
  "按体积算地球上最大的树，约 2,200 岁，比更老的红杉还大，是因为长在了水土最好的地方。": "The largest tree on Earth by volume, about 2,200 years old. It's bigger than older sequoias because it grew where the soil and water are best.",
  "沿悬崖边的台阶爬到岩顶，据说日落和夜景也很值得。": "Climb the stairs along the cliff edge to the top. Sunset and the night sky are said to be worth it too.",
  "景观道只在 4–11 月通车，开到公路尽头，能看出冰川磨出的宽阔 U 形谷。": "The byway is open only April–November. Drive to the end of the road and you can see the broad U-shaped valley carved by glaciers.",
  "先去游客中心看看有没有临时变动。": "Stop at a visitor center first to check for any temporary changes.",
  "Boyden 溶洞是私营的，每人约 $19、导游带 45–60 分钟，她觉得超级值。": "Boyden Cavern is privately run: about $19 per person for a 45–60-minute guided tour. She thought it was a great value.",
  "她在巨人森林看到黑熊爬上很高的树，注意保持距离。": "In Giant Forest she saw a black bear climb high up a tree. Keep your distance.",
  "老佳和老萌": "Lao Jia he Lao Meng",
  "4 月": "April",
  "一家三口从拉斯维加斯出发的 10 天西南小环线：死亡谷、火焰谷、锡安、Kanab、Page、鲍威尔湖、大峡谷，最后回拉斯维加斯。国家公园里的几晚都住园内，晚上出门看星空方便。": "A family of three on a 10-day Southwest loop from Las Vegas: Death Valley, Valley of Fire, Zion, Kanab, Page, Lake Powell, and the Grand Canyon, then back to Las Vegas. They stayed inside each national park, which made it easy to go out stargazing at night.",
